[E-MATCH-MOTIVE] Error: a `match` can't be used here: there is no definition to lift it into
   ╭─[ reject/match-in-type-declaration.sw:6:24 ]
   │
 6 │ type Box = | MkBox (n: match 1 with | 0 => Nat | Succ m => Nat)
   │                        ───────────────────┬───────────────────  
   │                                           ╰───────────────────── this `match`
   │ 
   │ Note 1: a `match` becomes a helper definition next to the definition it is in; a `type` or `ability` declaration has no definition to put one beside
   │ 
   │ Note 2: a top-level helper with a written signature can always do what this `match` would: define one and call it
───╯
